<%--
Api_Key_Scopes_Modal_Body - one existing key's scope, read-only.

Shows the canonical rule text and, beside it, the endpoints those rules actually reach -
resolved by <Api_Scope_Preview> against the real route table, the same panel and the same
resolver the mint form previews with.

READ-ONLY BY DESIGN. A key is immutable after mint: changing a credential already in service
would change what it can do under the integration holding it, silently. Narrowing a key means
revoking it and generating a replacement.

Arguments:
- $key_id (int, required): the key to describe. The endpoint refuses a key belonging to
  anybody else exactly as it refuses one that does not exist.

Usage:
    <Api_Key_Scopes_Modal_Body $key_id=7 />
--%>
<Define:Api_Key_Scopes_Modal_Body tag="div">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <label class="form-label fw-bold">Key Name</label>
        <div class="text-muted"><%= this.data.name %></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-3">
        <label class="form-label fw-bold">Rules</label>
        <% if (this.data.unrestricted) { %>
            <div class="text-muted">Unrestricted - this key carries every permission your account has.</div>
        <% } else { %>
            <pre class="Api_Key_Scopes_Modal_Body__rules"><%= this.data.scopes %></pre>
        <% } %>
    </div>

    <Api_Scope_Preview $scopes=this.data.scopes />
</Define:Api_Key_Scopes_Modal_Body>
